<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><h1 class="st-title">Colony of Saint Christopher</h1><p class="st-meta">1623 CE – 1882 CE · capital Basseterre</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">England's first colony in the Caribbean, founded on Saint Kitts in 1623, which served as the 'mother colony' of the English West Indies.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thomas-warner">Thomas Warner</a> landed on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-kitts">Saint Christopher</a> (Saint Kitts) with a small group of settlers in 1623, founding the first English colony in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a>. Arriving French settlers shared the island, and in 1626 the two groups massacred the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalinago">Kalinago</a> inhabitants at Bloody Point.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>From 1627 the island was partitioned, with the English holding the centre and the French the ends. English settlers spread from there to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/colony-of-nevis">Nevis</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/colony-of-antigua">Antigua</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/montserrat">Montserrat</a>. Tobacco gave way to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a>, worked by enslaved Africans. The English and French fought repeatedly over the island, and from 1671 it belonged to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/leeward-islands-colony">Leeward Islands colony</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-utrecht">Treaty of Utrecht</a> in 1713 gave <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> the whole island. The French captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brimstone-hill-fortress">Brimstone Hill</a> in 1782 but returned it in 1783. In 1882 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-kitts">Saint Christopher</a> was joined with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/colony-of-nevis">Nevis</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anguilla">Anguilla</a> as <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/saint-christopher-nevis-anguilla">Saint Christopher-Nevis-Anguilla</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="colony, 1623 CE – 1882 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 64 H80 L70 78 H30 Z"/><path d="M50 64 V18"/><path d="M50 22 L72 56 H50"/><path d="M50 28 L32 56 H50"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">colony</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:92.00%;width:5.15%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1623 CE – 1882 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Basseterre</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Thomas Warner</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Anglicanism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>English</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/saint-kitts-and-nevis">Saint Kitts and Nevis</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>English Saint Kitts, Saint Kitts</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1752&amp;focus=colony-of-saint-christopher" aria-label="Colony of Saint Christopher on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2975 1535 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Colony of Saint Christopher lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M3295 1791L4997 651M3295 1791L3320 1799M3295 1791L3295 1791M3295 1791L3295 1791"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4997 651h0M3320 1799h0M3295 1791h0M3295 1791h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M3295 1791h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M3295 1791h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Basseterre. <a href="/atlas?year=1752&amp;focus=colony-of-saint-christopher">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
